{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559231-the-mal-akhim-of-the-heavenly-host-2-0-scion-2e-hombrew-pantheon-update","id":1559231,"title":"The Mal'akhim of the Heavenly Host 2.0 [Scion 2e hombrew Pantheon update]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-05T08:18:32-07:00","id":1559231,"title":"The Mal'akhim of the Heavenly Host 2.0 [Scion 2e hombrew Pantheon update]","content":"Officialy re-releasing my homebrew Abrahamic Pantheon, which I had previously posted in this forum. <br /> Changelog:<ul><li>Added a rudimentary Pronunciation Guide sidebar at the start on Biblical Hebrew, Classical Arabic, Ecclesiastical Latin and Koine Greek.</li> <li>Shuffled some sidebars around and/or folding them into main parts and/or separated them into smaller ones.</li> <li>The entire Titans section was relocated to after the Cosmology section.</li> <li>Many various incremental edits within the intro, Principal Members, Primordial, Cosmology, Titans and Religions sections. Can't remember them all in detail, but of note: some Archangels and Archdemons had superfluous Purviews removed; some of their flavor texts and that of YHWH were either rephrased, expanded (notably Zadkiel's) or reworked entirely; the Duidain write-up in Midrealms was shortened and folded into the Eden description; and the Religions section was reworked and expanded with additional lore.</li> <li>On the side of Birthrights: flavor texts all throughout were given incremental edits; re'em as a Creature, as well as rabbi/ministers/imams as Guide and flying carpets and Solomonic bottles as Relics, were removed for feeling like not unique enough to warrant an entire write-up; all remaining Creatures and Followers and some remaining Relics were given reworked and/or expanded stat sheets; some Guides were reworked; and added descriptive flavor text on how the Mal'akhim and their Scions interact with Covenants and Creeds; a brand-new Cult section was also added, with full write-ups for example Abrahamic Cults, including Templar Holdings (which used to be list as a Guide), the Asasiyyun and the Catholic Church.</li> <li>Relationships section was entirely overhauled.</li> <li>The PSP has a different Motif, the &quot;Be Not Afraid&quot; Boon was removed and the gives-angel-wings-at-Tier4 side of its effect was folded into the Innate Power. A brand new Boon &quot;Vade Retro&quot; was added to replace Be Not Afraid.</li> <li>All Example Antagonists were completely reworked, and few brand new ones were added: say hello to the ifrit, Legion, the Golem of Prague and Astaroth!</li> <li>In the New Denizen Paths section, Winged Variant: Angel had its Calling Keywords, Path Contacts and Persistent Condition updated, and Sphinx Variant: Cherub was removed and was replaced by the brand-new standalone Hell-Born.</li> </ul><br /> Here's the link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pGY-eaFQJRqmvYRZLMtR84Vb_63LFnY9e7A7K1zSi20/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>. Please, provide feedback within this forum post, I'll be grateful if you do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-05T11:24:27-07:00","id":1559232,"title":"","content":"In the God Player's Guide, the Born, Created, Chosen, and Incarnated Scions are joined by a fifth type: Simply Divine. These are Scions who were never Heroes or Demigods and started out as Gods. Among the Mal'akhim, this would almost entirely replace the Born, and would compete with the Chosen as the most common type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-05T12:41:23-07:00","id":1559233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559231-the-mal-akhim-of-the-heavenly-host-2-0-scion-2e-hombrew-pantheon-update?p=1559232#post1559232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the God Player's Guide, the Born, Created, Chosen, and Incarnated Scions are joined by a fifth type: Simply Divine. These are Scions who were never Heroes or Demigods and started out as Gods. Among the Mal'akhim, this would almost entirely replace the Born, and would compete with the Chosen as the most common type.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026 yes, and? First of all, God Player\u2019s Guide explicitly presents Simply Divine as an Origin Path, not a Scion type. And second of all, well, that\u2019s the thing: a Simply Divine character doesn\u2019t count as a Scion to begin with, because by definition, they never were one. And it\u2019s not like the Archangels CAN have normal Born Scions anyway, due to the mandatory chastity and the whole &quot;Nephilim&quot; thing. So, no offense, but I don\u2019t get what issue you\u2019re trying to call out here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-05T13:13:39-07:00","id":1559234,"title":"","content":"I missed the bit that it's an Origin Path. That said, the document should point out that the vast majority of Angels <i>have </i>that Origin Path: you kind of mention that when you say that YHWH can simply make more of them whenever he wants; but an explicit reference to Simply Divine would be appropriate at that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T09:18:10-07:00","id":1559246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559231-the-mal-akhim-of-the-heavenly-host-2-0-scion-2e-hombrew-pantheon-update?p=1559234#post1559234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I missed the bit that it's an Origin Path. That said, the document should point out that the vast majority of Angels <i>have </i>that Origin Path: you kind of mention that when you say that YHWH can simply make more of them whenever he wants; but an explicit reference to Simply Divine would be appropriate at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get your point, but I don't think it's necessary. Unless I'm remembering wrong, the fact that most Gods are Simply Divine is implictly already the norm amongst most other Pantheons, so the Archangels aren't really all that unique on that front. And besides, the &quot;Simply Divine&quot; Origin Path is only relevant in the very specific context of God-tier character creation, and it has not predefinite Path Skills or Connections, so it's not like it has any real mechanical impact anyway.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, any other feedback on the homebrew?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T11:47:17-07:00","id":1559416,"title":"","content":"Very nice idea and very well made ^^<br /> <br /> Altough in my personal opinion, did I understand that correctly and in your version they are the by far biggest Pantheon?<br /> <br /> Becaus I think even the deva and Chinese Pantheon are already too big and powerful. In a world where all gods and religions are true I think no Pantheon will watch idly by while one othet grows even bigger and bigger. And they will likely band together and fight against one that gets too powerful.<br /> <br /> Therefore I think no Pantheon should ever grow over the nearly one billion followers worldwide size and even that maybe even already too big. Altough that's only my personal opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28820-akhelos","name":"Akhelos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T01:17:46-07:00","id":1559424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akhelos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559231-the-mal-akhim-of-the-heavenly-host-2-0-scion-2e-hombrew-pantheon-update?p=1559416#post1559416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very nice idea and very well made ^^<br /> <br /> Altough in my personal opinion, did I understand that correctly and in your version they are the by far biggest Pantheon?<br /> <br /> Becaus I think even the deva and Chinese Pantheon are already too big and powerful. In a world where all gods and religions are true I think no Pantheon will watch idly by while one othet grows even bigger and bigger. And they will likely band together and fight against one that gets too powerful.<br /> <br /> Therefore I think no Pantheon should ever grow over the nearly one billion followers worldwide size and even that maybe even already too big. Altough that's only my personal opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried my best not to make the Mal'akhim seem too much like Mary Sues <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> although I'm only taking the real-life religions into account. IRL, Christianity and Islam both individually have more numbers than Hinduism, and together represent over a half of the entire world's population. Even taking into account the comparative loss of numbers in Scion's World, this would still put the Abrahamic Pantheon on par with the Dev\u00e1 at the very least. And because the course of The World's history is assumed to be the same as ours in the broad strokes, you need to take into account all the events that happened BECAUSE of the Abrahamic religions' dominance, and how somehow, the Mal'akhim managed to stay a top-dog Pantheon all the way to the current day without getting wiped out by those who might gang up on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T02:54:50-07:00","id":1559425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akhelos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559231-the-mal-akhim-of-the-heavenly-host-2-0-scion-2e-hombrew-pantheon-update?p=1559416#post1559416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very nice idea and very well made ^^<br /> <br /> Altough in my personal opinion, did I understand that correctly and in your version they are the by far biggest Pantheon?<br /> <br /> Becaus I think even the deva and Chinese Pantheon are already too big and powerful. In a world where all gods and religions are true I think no Pantheon will watch idly by while one othet grows even bigger and bigger. And they will likely band together and fight against one that gets too powerful.<br /> <br /> Therefore I think no Pantheon should ever grow over the nearly one billion followers worldwide size and even that maybe even already too big. Altough that's only my personal opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of them probably just don't care.<br /> <br /> If it's a setting where &quot;Faith=Power&quot; and worshipers are viewed only as a resource, then sure, the other Pantheons wouldn't allow that one monotheistic cult from the Middle East to ever get so popular, but that's not really <i><b>Scion</b></i>'s setting.<br /> <br /> There's no guarantee that a Pantheon with a larger number of followers are automatically stronger than one with less.<br /> <br /> The Gods aren't tied to the number of mortals that worship them.<br /> <br /> Unless the Mal'akhim decided to sound the horns of war and hold crusade against polytheistic religions, commanding their followers to defile temples, destroys idols and relics, or force people to convert or die (and ACTUALLY following up on that - not just being distant figures in the background while the operation was planned and executed by their human followers for their own agendas like the times before), I doubt the remaining Pantheons would be able to put aside their differences and personal history for the sake of a glorified popularity contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27963-jayng2183","name":"JayNg2183","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27963_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T05:40:42-07:00","id":1559501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559231-the-mal-akhim-of-the-heavenly-host-2-0-scion-2e-hombrew-pantheon-update?p=1559424#post1559424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried my best not to make the Mal'akhim seem too much like Mary Sues <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> although I'm only taking the real-life religions into account. IRL, Christianity and Islam both individually have more numbers than Hinduism, and together represent over a half of the entire world's population. Even taking into account the comparative loss of numbers in Scion's World, this would still put the Abrahamic Pantheon on par with the Dev\u00e1 at the very least. And because the course of The World's history is assumed to be the same as ours in the broad strokes, you need to take into account all the events that happened BECAUSE of the Abrahamic religions' dominance, and how somehow, the Mal'akhim managed to stay a top-dog Pantheon all the way to the current day without getting wiped out by those who might gang up on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Altough that would mean the abrahamic, celestial bureaucracy and deva have all around one billion followers each and control half of humanities population. If these three work together they could rule the world. ^^<br /> Altough could also be a fun setting where the whole overlord is ruled by a triumvirate of these three. <br /> <br /> And at least my first edition scion of Indra who was later converted to second edition always reminded everyone how big her pantheon is......yes she is very arrogant. ^^<br /> &quot;The Indian diaspora worldwide alone has 32 million people, my family has totally over a billion followers. How many thousand does your tiny pantheon have again?&quot; ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28820-akhelos","name":"Akhelos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}